    {
      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/22-spiny-eels/synbranchus_marmoratus_en/",
      "html": "<p>Synbranchus marmoratus can hardly be called a beauty in the conventional sense, but even the extraordinary has its attraction. At the moment, besides swamp eels in \"normal\" sizes, a giant of approximately 1 m length is also available.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/22-spiny-eels/synbranchus_marmoratus_en/",
      "html": "<p>Mexico - Argentina, Peru</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "equipment",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/22-spiny-eels/synbranchus_marmoratus_en/",
      "html": "<p>To avoid unpleasant nocturnal meetings, the aquarium should be hermetically closed.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "behaviour",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/22-spiny-eels/synbranchus_marmoratus_en/",
      "html": "<p>Of course, a predator of this size should not be kept together with small \"food fishes\". In addition, they try to undertake nocturnal migrations.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "notes",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/22-spiny-eels/synbranchus_marmoratus_en/",
      "html": "<p>For those looking for an alternative to the usual community tank, it might be an interesting ornamental fish.</p>"
    }
  ],
